ut you can have  fun again  and so that's really what people are  coming back to our properties and that's  what that's what's bringing them out  here and  back to las vegas and so it's just  really exciting to see that to see that  excitement again to see  people out here having fun again and  getting back to what we do best here in  las vegas  when you think about this unprecedented  time what was maybe  the biggest challenge and how did you  transcend it as a company  back when we first talked last year at  the suncoast  we didn't really know what to expect  right i mean this was unprecedented  territory we were reopening our business  from ground from ground zero we had to  introduce all of these safety protocols  because you know you had to keep people  safe  and so that meant doing things like  social distancing it meant  making people wear masks when they come  into your property uh it meant cleaning  everything constantly so you're cleaning  chips constantly you're cleaning  chairs constantly slot machine buttons  so this is just an entire  level of complexity that we never had to  do before  and at the same time our team members  have to be out there  giving their a game because people are  still coming here  they still want to have fun and so they  still have to to  to deliver that experience that our  customers wanted you know what they did  it  they did it they couldn't have done it  better and they kept it going throughout  the whole pandemic and  and brought us to where we're at here  today we couldn't have done it without  them  when you look at your team members i  imagine it's a collective point of pride  talk a little bit about what you think  about what the boyd gaming team did  working together to get through this and  now being able to enjoy some level of  normalcy yeah i mean  look that was such we were asking so  much of them right  because the job itself is already a  challenge you're already focused 100  on giving that great experience all t